---
// Explainer: one named ETF, separating the total estimate from component fee limits.
---
<figure class="fee-map" data-card="figure" aria-labelledby="fee-map-title">
  <figcaption id="fee-map-title"><strong>Korea ETF: the total estimate and the two fee layers</strong></figcaption>
  <p class="fee-map-name">iFAST Xtrackers MSCI Korea UCITS Index ETF (SGX: KOR)</p>

  <div class="fee-map-total">
    <span class="fee-map-label">Published estimate · not a cap</span>
    <b>0.67% a year</b>
    <span>About S$67 a year on a constant S$10,000 holding</span>
    <p>This is the estimated total expense ratio (TER). It is a total, not another charge to add to the fees below. Brokerage and currency conversion are extra.</p>
    <p class="fee-map-source"><a href="https://fsm.global/sg/article/rcms397520">FSM Global, Table 1</a> · data at 29 September 2026 · publisher estimate, not an audited actual cost.</p>
  </div>

  <p><strong>The prospectus describes two layers.</strong> Their fee limits explain what can be charged; they are not a breakdown that adds up to the 0.67% estimate.</p>
  <div class="fee-map-grid">
    <section aria-label="Singapore fund fees">
      <h3>1. Singapore: the iFAST fund</h3>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Management fee <span class="fee-map-label">Current charge</span></dt><dd>0.25% a year<span class="fee-map-label">Maximum: 0.90% a year for this fee only</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Other running expenses <span class="fee-map-label">Combined amount not stated</span></dt><dd>Additional</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>Custodian, registrar and administrator fees may each reach or exceed 0.10% a year. That is not a combined 0.10% allowance or cap.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-label="Underlying Xtrackers fund fees">
      <h3>2. Overseas: the fund it holds</h3>
      <p class="fee-map-fund">Xtrackers MSCI Korea UCITS ETF, Class 1C</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Management company fee <span class="fee-map-label">Stated upper limit</span></dt><dd>Up to 0.25% a year</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Fixed fee <span class="fee-map-label">Stated fixed charge</span></dt><dd>0.20% a year</dd></div>
        <div class="fee-map-subtotal"><dt>Underlying all-in fee <span class="fee-map-label">Includes both rows above</span></dt><dd>Up to 0.45% a year</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>The 0.20% fixed fee belongs to this overseas fund. The 0.45% limit covers this layer, not the whole iFAST ETF.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="fee-map-source"><a href="https://links.sgx.com/FileOpen/iFAST%20Global%20ETFs%20Select%20Series%20VCC%20-%20Amended%20Prospectus.ashx?App=IPO&amp;FileID=6796">iFAST prospectus</a>, registered 29 September 2026, Korea sections 6C–6D, printed pages 180–181. Each percentage uses the assets of the fund charging it.</p>
  <p class="fee-map-caution"><strong>No overall TER cap found.</strong> The publisher does not explain how its 0.67% estimate reconciles with these components. We do not assume a rebate or subsidy. Actual total expenses may differ.</p>
  <p><strong>These are fund expenses, not a separate iFAST platform bill.</strong> A unit-trust platform may charge a separate service fee on top of its fund’s expenses; that is a different arrangement.</p>
</figure>
<style>
